#!/usr/bin/env rexx
/* File:        05-client-clr.rxj
 * Description: Creates a networking client which connects to a server listening on address 127.0.0.1
 *              (localhost) and port 2015. User input is sent to the server.
 *              Note: Sending a message to any other program than "05-server-clr.rexp" listening on
 *              this port by chance might cause unpredictable behavior.
 * Shows:       - Instantiation of classes (without parameters)
 *              - Invokation of methods (with/without parameters)
 *              - Retrieval of properties
 *
 * Needs:       05-server-clr.rxj must be running in another command line window/process, before
 *              this program is executed (otherwise the peer server cannot be contacted)
 *
 * Changed: ---rgf, 2016-06-25
 *              - use UTF8-encoding, such that non-ASCII-characters can be transported
 *
 * License:
 *
 *  ------------------------ Apache Version 2.0 license -------------------------
 *     Copyright (C) 2015 Manuel Raffel
 *     Copyright (C) 2016 Rony G. Flatscher
 *
 *     Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
 *     you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
 *     You may obtain a copy of the License at
 *
 *         http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
 *
 *     Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
 *     distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
 *     WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
 *     See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
 *     limitations under the License.
 *  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

tcpClient = .clr~new("System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient")  -- create instance of class "System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient"

SAY "Connecting to 127.0.0.1:2015..."
tcpClient~Connect("127.0.0.1", 2015)   -- connect "TcpClient" to specified address ("localhost") and port (2015)
SAY "Connected."

SAY "Input message to server:"
PARSE PULL message   -- fetch message from user
   -- encode message as UTF8 and return a byte array representing it
encodedMessage = clr.import("System.Text.Encoding")~UTF8~GetBytes(message)  -- convert input into byte array

SAY "Sending message..."
tcpClient~GetStream~Write(encodedMessage, 0, encodedMessage~Length)  -- send encoded message to server
SAY "Message was sent to server."

tcpClient~Close  -- close TCP connection

::REQUIRES CLR.CLS  -- get ooRexx.NET support